@@ -0,0 +1,165 @@
+# v2 spawn feel — terminal-spawn telegraph + reveal (no more instant pops)
+
+User complaint #3: a terminal spawn is an **instant pop with zero telegraph**.
+The growth director lands a node at the 80-tick window and `draw_building` just
+draws whatever exists — no announcement, no reveal. This PR gives the board a
+readable spawn moment, plus folds the estate-spawning r1 follow-up warnings
+(jint_strict seed floor, 134 test bad-frees, the diameter-guard bound).
+
+## The spawn moment (view-layer only, tick-anchored)
+
+Three beats around the growth tick T (the 08-21 pace cadence: one spawn per
+4 s — the rate job landed first, so the reveal reads at the 80-tick window per
+briefing rule 3):
+
+1. **Telegraph (T-10 → T, 0.5 s pre-pop)** — a soft expanding white ring at
+   the NEXT spawn's position. The position is **predicted by stepping a
+   shadow copy of the sim** to the window: the sim is fully deterministic
+   (seed-derived; the rng draws come only from flow + growth), so the shadow
+   replays the identical rng draws and the prediction is bit-exact — the
+   player sees *where* the next terminal will appear before it lands
+   (cause→effect).
+2. **Reveal (T → T+8, 0.4 s)** — the landed node's sprite scales 0.4→1.0 and
+   fades in (the shadow + wash + chip ride the same transform); the ring
+   bursts outward + fades across the same window.
+3. **Placement (T → T+4, 0.2 s)** — the pipes within 8 tiles of the new node
+   pulse a translucent glow band ("this node just joined the network").
+   Interpretation note: a freshly spawned terminal has NO pipes yet, so the
+   highlight covers its neighborhood's pipes (the estate it joined) — the
+   nearest honest reading of "the connecting pipe" in this sim.
+
+All three are **pure functions of (tick, effect state)** — the §10.4
+determinism rule: no transcendentals in the raster path (the ring is a pinned
+36-point table annulus, smoothstep easing), captures at the same ticks stay
+reproducible, and **sim-validity timing is unchanged** (the node is
+gameplay-valid at the growth tick; the reveal is cosmetic timing only — no
+sim state written, T1 hashes byte-identical, LOG_VERSION untouched).
+
+**The shadow predictor** (`app/render/spawn_fx.odin`): a deep clone of
+Run_State stepped forward ≤10 ticks with the caller's pending commands.
+Pinned by tests: clone round-trips hash-identical (a missed field diverges
+the telegraph), the predicted position EQUALS the actual spawn, and a pending
+draw moves the prediction exactly like the live sim. The app predicts once
+per window + re-predicts when a player edit bumps the topology gen mid-window
+(the ring retargets within a frame); the harness re-predicts per capture —
+both are pure functions of the same state, so they agree bit-for-bit.
+
+**Event authority**: the reveal is fed from the NODE_SPAWNED event stream
+(the same mark-based slice the audio consumer reads — never drained, the 4.2
+tripwire). Node identification is via E11 monotonic ids (the event has zero
+payload); a same-tick telegraph retargets onto the landed node.
+
+**rlsw traps handled**: the ring + highlight are FILLS (the software
+renderer ignores line alpha), and the triangles are CCW — rlgl enables
+backface culling with front = CCW, so a CW annulus renders nothing in BOTH
+the captures and the GPU app (caught by the first save, fixed, re-blessed).
+
+**Reduced-motion (E9.2)**: the ring pins to a static mid-radius presence,
+the reveal is instant, the highlight steady — the pulse_read precedent
+(presence, not motion).
+
+**Cadence-pacing signal (briefing item 4)**: the premise did not survive —
+the 2 s cadence became 4 s (the pace job landed), so steady streams are
+sparse and the fatigue-variation is moot. The constants live in one place
+(`SPAWN_*_TICKS`) so a future cadence knob retunes them together.
+
+## Estate-spawning r1 follow-up folds (relayed via Silas)
+
+1. **`new_area_seed_tiles` now parses `jint_strict`** (`core/catalog.odin`)
+   — a decimal (10.5) silently truncated and an out-of-i32 value wrapped,
+   and this key feeds the diameter guard: a wrapped value could pass the
+   bound with a wrong floor. Added the decimal rejection row (10.5) to
+   catalog_test.
+2. **134 `+++ bad free` per `odin test core` run eliminated** — the
+   `strict_spawn_class` test helper did `make([]i32, n, context.temp_allocator)`
+   + `defer delete(...)` (invalid frees — the temp arena owns the memory),
+   drowning genuine tracker output. Dropped the two defers. Verified: the
+   count is now 2, both pre-existing in untouched `health_test.odin`
+   (out of this PR's scope, noted for whoever touches that file).
+3. **The diameter guard now rejects never-clearable floors** — the bound is
+   the widest ACHIEVABLE spacing, `(w-1)²+(h-1)²`, not the raw `w²+h²`
+   diagonal: on 40×30 the old check accepted `new_area_seed_tiles: 49`
+   (49² = 2401 > 2362 = 39²+29² — the far corner-to-corner distance), a
+   floor no candidate could ever clear → every growth window exhausts the
+   rejection budget and stalls silently. Now: 49/50/51 reject; the boundary
+   48 loads clean AND is asserted (the r1 note: the parsed value was never
+   asserted — only reject rows existed).
+
+## Golden re-bless (deliberate, cause-documented)
+
+- **`node_health` 20000ms** — the capture tick lands exactly on a growth
+  window (t400); the frame now carries the reveal at age 0 (the new node at
+  scale 0.4/fade 0.3 + the ring burst + the highlight). 00050/10000ms are
+  byte-identical to the blessed frames (no window overlap).
+- **`growth` 88000ms** — audited: t1760 is a window but the plan rejected
+  that window (no spawn), so the frame is byte-identical — NO re-bless.
+- **New `spawn_feel.dem`** (9 captures across two windows: pre-ring at ages
+  2/8, the pop, reveal mid/tail/settled, the second window's telegraph +
+  pop — the 4 s cadence beat). Every blessed log re-sims its manifest
+  bit-for-bit; the full suite is 47/47 green.
+- No other demo's captures fall inside a telegraph/reveal window (checked
+  every growth-enabled demo's capture ticks against the 80-tick grid).
+
+## Rebase onto v2 (post-#82/#85 wave ripple, 2026-08-22)
+
+Rebased onto the fresh v2 head (motion-readability #82 + noc-overlay #85
+merged). Conflict resolved: the View gained #82's `pkt_interp` field and my
+`spawn_fx` field side-by-side (both presentation-only). Regenerated the two
+goldens that share the packet-trail render class on the combined baseline:
+`node_health-20000` and `spawn_feel` 07600/07900/08000 (the diff vs the
+pre-rebase goldens is exactly the #82 trail rings on in-flight packets — the
+spawn-feel content itself, ring center + reveal envelope, is byte-identical
+pre/post rebase). `spawn_feel.t1` is untouched (the manifest format did not
+change — #85 only refactored the writer). Full suite: **48/48 demos green**
+(47 + the new motion.dem), **11/11 CI gates green**.
+
+## Perkins r1 fold (review 5001127448)
+
+- **B1 (fixed)**: the pipe-highlight radius mixed UNITS — `rad = 8 tiles ×
+  tile_px` (208 px) compared against tile-unit distances, so no pipe on a
+  40×30 map could ever be excluded and EVERY spawn flashed the whole
+  network (golden-verified: the 04000ms frame pulsed pipe 1→3 at 9.8 tiles
+  from the spawn). Fixed to compare tile units; re-blessed the three
+  highlight-bearing spawn_feel frames + node_health-20000 (the pre-fix vs
+  post-fix diff is exactly the removed far-pipe band, x 656→960 at the
+  pipe's y — the local estate-pipe highlight is unchanged).
+- **B2 (fixed)**: the pending-commands test was vacuous — the fixture draw
+  0→3 spans 25 > the standard tier's max_span 14, so it was rejected on
+  both sides and the assertion was a tautology. Reworked: the pending
+  command is now a legal router place at (13,6) that BLOCKS the no-pending
+  spawn [10,6] (3 tiles — inside the E31 4-tile node-separation floor),
+  with an ANTI-VACUITY assert (the no-pending prediction must land
+  elsewhere — a shadow that dropped the pending slice now fails the test),
+  a materialization assert (the place must land + not latch replay_error),
+  and the NEGATIVE leg (an out-of-separation place is rejected on both
+  sides and the prediction still matches).
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+| Decision | Why |
+|---|---|
+| Shadow-sim prediction (clone + ≤10-step replay) for the telegraph | The ONLY way to draw the ring at the next spawn's position before it lands, in a fully deterministic sim — and it is bit-exact + T2-stable by construction. Rejected: post-hoc ring (fails "pre→pop"), core-side prediction (would change sim semantics — rule 1), prediction without the shadow (the rng draws between windows come from flow — not predictably derivable). |
+| Prediction lives in the render package | View-layer only (rule 1): the shadow is a read-only deep copy; nothing in core changes; the growth tick is untouched. The clone is pinned hash-identical by a test. |
+| Zero-payload NODE_SPAWNED event kept | Changing the event payload would shift the serialized event stream + T1 hashes (a sim-observable change — the briefing's rule 1). E11 monotonic ids identify the node without it. |
+| Ring/highlight as filled geometry (pinned table + quads), not lines | The rlsw software renderer ignores line alpha — a fading line would capture solid. |
+| CCW triangle winding | rlgl enables GL_BACK culling with front = CCW — CW triangles render nothing on BOTH the software captures and the GPU app (caught + fixed during the first save). |
+| Pipe-highlight scope = pipes within 8 tiles of the node | A fresh spawn has no pipes; the estate it joined is the honest "network it connected to". |
+| Reveal fade floor 0.3 (not 0) | The node is gameplay-valid at T — a fully invisible node read as a bug; 0.3 keeps the pop readable from its first tick while still telegraphing "new". |
+| Reduced-motion: static ring + instant reveal | The E9.2 precedent (pulse pinned static, presence retained). |
+| Cadence variation (briefing item 4) not implemented | Premise gone: the cadence is 4 s, not 2 s — steady streams don't fatigue. Noted for the future if a faster cadence returns. |
+| `sprite_blit`/wash/chip gained default params instead of new procs | Backward-compatible call sites; one transform threaded through the whole node draw. |
+
+## Verification
+
+- `odin test core`: 236/236 (bad-frees 134 → 2 pre-existing)
+- `odin test app/render`: 22/22 (7 new spawn-fx pins: clone round-trip,
+  predict == actual spawn, pending-commands path, negatives, feed walk-back,
+  reveal math, dedup)
+- `tools/harness.sh run`: **47/47 demos green** (T1 manifests + T2 pixels +
+  replay gate + fold-check)
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac`: **10/10 gates green** (incl. input-parity 27/27)
+- Capture sequence (mechanical pixel audit): ring grows 3600→3900ms, pop at
+  4000ms (node at scale 0.4 + highlight band to the estate uplink), reveal
+  footprint grows monotonically to full at 4400ms, second beat at 7600/8000ms.
+  Visual aesthetic verdict deferred to the human/Kyle review (the vision
+  model was rate-limited during the run; the golden bytes are deterministic).
