new file mode 100644
index 00000000..20f6cfe7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/spawn_feel.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# spawn_feel.dem — v2-spawn-feel's named golden: the terminal-spawn TELEGRAPH
+# + REVEAL capture sequence (the user's complaint #3 — "a terminal spawn is
+# an INSTANT POP with zero telegraph"). The recipe is growth.dem's proven
+# era-1 setup (seed 42, fixture + a player-placed router at 1000 ms + two
+# draws at 2000/2500 ms — the mesh growth grows outward from), shortened to
+# 16 s: four 80-tick windows (the pace-tuning cadence, 4 s apart).
+#
+# The captures walk ONE spawn window pre→pop→settle (t80 = 4000 ms — the
+# first spawn) + the second window's telegraph (t160 = 8000 ms):
+#
+#   3600 ms (t72)  — the telegraph RING, age 2: soft expanding annulus at the
+#                    landing spot, BEFORE the node exists (the shadow-sim
+#                    prediction — deterministic, same seed -> same position)
+#   3900 ms (t78)  — the ring at full pre-pop radius (age 8)
+#   4000 ms (t80)  — THE POP: the node lands gameplay-valid; the reveal
+#                    starts (scale 0.4 / fade 0.3), the ring bursts, the
+#                    nearby pipes pulse the placement highlight
+#   4100 ms (t82)  — reveal mid-envelope (scale ~0.75, fade ~0.8)
+#   4250 ms (t85)  — reveal tail (the node ~settled, highlight fading)
+#   4400 ms (t88)  — settled: the node reads like any other (reveal done)
+#   7600 ms (t152) — the SECOND window's telegraph (age 2 — the cadence beat)
+#   7900 ms (t158) — the second ring at full radius
+#   8000 ms (t160) — the second pop (the cadence reveal reads at the 4 s
+#                    cadence — the briefing's rule 3 verification)
+#
+# Determinism: growth is seed-derived (no action-log entries), the shadow
+# prediction is a pure function of the same state, and the reveal is tick-
+# anchored from the growth tick — same seed -> byte-identical captures.
+seed 42
+era 1
+run 16000ms
+growth on
+at 1000ms place router_basic 34 15
+at 2000ms draw 1 3 standard
+at 2500ms draw 0 1 standard
+capture at 3600ms
+capture at 3900ms
+capture at 4000ms
+capture at 4100ms
+capture at 4250ms
+capture at 4400ms
+capture at 7600ms
+capture at 7900ms
+capture at 8000ms
+expect hash stable
